# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# ROOT CAUSE OF THE S00-B IMAGE DEFECT: with no .dockerignore, the host repository's macOS
# /Apple Silicon .venv entered the build context, and `COPY . .` after `uv sync` overwrote
# the Linux .venv the image had just built. Inside the pod that left
# /repo/.venv/bin/python -> /opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.13/bin/python3.13, a dangling symlink,
# so the project interpreter did not execute and torch was unimportable.
#
# Host-generated environments and caches must never enter the image. The authoritative
# environment is the one `uv sync --frozen` builds INSIDE the image [AUTH: 01 §12].

# host virtualenvs — the defect above
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv

# host tool caches
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# host OS noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT excluded. The image ships /repo as a real pinned worktree so
# scripts/bootstrap_runpod_s00b.sh can run `git rev-parse HEAD`, verify the exact required
# commit and enforce the clean-tree gate inside the pod [AUTH: 01 §35(3), §36; plan §8.1].
